2026-01-23 22:11:46.116 | DEBUG    | Model response tool call: {"tool_name": "create_file", "args": "{\"file_path\": \"/teamspace/studios/this_studio/arkan/dynamic-flows-studio/README.md\", \"initial_content\": \"# Dynamic Flows Studio\\n\\nA standalone, powerful workflow automation platform for building and executing complex dynamic flows with an intuitive visual interface.\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 Features\\n\\n- **Visual Flow Builder**: Drag-and-drop interface to design complex workflows\\n- **Dynamic Execution**: Execute flows with real-time monitoring and logging\\n- **Advanced Conditions**: Support for conditional logic, loops, and complex branching\\n- **Step Handlers**: Flexible step execution with custom handlers\\n- **Template Engine**: Built-in template processing for dynamic content\\n- **Schema Validation**: Automatic validation of flow schemas\\n- **API Integration**: RESTful API for flow management and execution\\n- **Real-time Monitoring**: Monitor flow execution with performance metrics\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce6 Project Structure\\n\\n```\\ndynamic-flows-studio/\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 ai/\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 dynamic-flow/          # Core flow execution engine\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 flows/                 # Flow executors and implementations\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 schemas/               # Type definitions and schemas\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 lib/\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 cache/                 # Caching mechanisms\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 models/                # Data models\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 utils/                 # Utility functions\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 services/                  # Business logic services\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 components/\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 builder/               # Flow builder components\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 executor/              # Flow executor UI\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 demo/                  # Demo components\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 ui/                    # Shared UI components\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 app/\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 api/                   # API routes\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 builder/               # Builder page\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 demo/                  # Demo page\\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 layout.tsx             # Root layout\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 hooks/                     # React hooks\\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 types/                     # TypeScript type definitions\\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 __tests__/                 # Test files\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 docs/                          # Documentation\\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 scripts/                       # Utility scripts\\n```\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Installation\\n\\n### Prerequisites\\n- Node.js 18.x or higher\\n- npm or pnpm\\n\\n### Setup\\n\\n1. Install dependencies:\\n```bash\\nnpm install\\n# or\\npnpm install\\n```\\n\\n2. Create environment file (`.env.local`):\\n```bash\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_key\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your_domain\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your_bucket\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your_sender_id\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your_app_id\\n```\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 Getting Started\\n\\n### Development\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run dev\\n```\\n\\nVisit `http://localhost:3000` to start building flows.\\n\\n### Build\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run build\\nnpm start\\n```\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcda Key Components\\n\\n### Dynamic Flow Engine\\nThe core execution engine located in `src/ai/dynamic-flow/`:\\n\\n- **Executor**: Main flow execution orchestrator\\n- **Context Manager**: Manages flow context and state\\n- **Condition Evaluator**: Evaluates conditions and branching logic\\n- **Step Executor**: Executes individual steps\\n- **Template Engine**: Processes templates and dynamic content\\n- **Schema Validator**: Validates flow configurations\\n\\n### Flow Builder UI\\nLocated in `src/components/builder/`:\\n\\n- Visual node-based interface\\n- Drag-and-drop connections\\n- Real-time validation\\n- Flow export/import\\n\\n### Flow Executor UI\\nLocated in `src/components/executor/`:\\n\\n- Real-time execution monitoring\\n- Performance metrics\\n- Execution logs\\n- Error tracking\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd17 API Endpoints\\n\\n### Admin Endpoints\\n- `POST /api/admin/flows` - Create flow\\n- `GET /api/admin/flows` - List flows\\n- `GET /api/admin/flows/[flowId]` - Get flow details\\n- `PUT /api/admin/flows/[flowId]` - Update flow\\n- `DELETE /api/admin/flows/[flowId]` - Delete flow\\n- `POST /api/admin/flows/[flowId]/execute` - Execute flow\\n\\n### Public Endpoints\\n- `POST /api/flows/execute` - Execute published flow\\n- `POST /api/flows/test` - Test flow execution\\n\\n## \ud83e\uddea Testing\\n\\n### Run Tests\\n```bash\\nnpm run test\\n```\\n\\n### Run Tests in Watch Mode\\n```bash\\nnpm run test:watch\\n```\\n\\n### Generate Coverage Report\\n```bash\\nnpm run test:coverage\\n```\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcd6 Documentation\\n\\nSee the `/docs` directory for:\\n- [Dynamic Flows Guide](./docs/dynamic-flows.md)\\n- [Quick Start](./docs/QUICK_START_DYNAMIC_FLOWS.md)\\n\\n## \ud83e\udd1d Contributing\\n\\n1. Create a feature branch\\n2. Make your changes\\n3. Run tests: `npm run test`\\n4. Run linter: `npm run lint`\\n5. Submit a pull request\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcdd License\\n\\nThis project is part of the Arkan ecosystem.\\n\\n## \ud83c\udd98 Support\\n\\nFor issues and questions:\\n1. Check the documentation\\n2. Review existing issues\\n3. Create a new issue with details\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd04 Migration from Arkan\\n\\nThis project was extracted from the Arkan project to provide a focused, standalone Dynamic Flows experience. All core functionality has been preserved with the following structure:\\n\\n- Core engine: `src/ai/dynamic-flow/`\\n- Flow executors: `src/ai/flows/`\\n- Services: `src/services/`\\n- Models: `src/lib/models/`\\n- API routes: `src/app/api/`\\n- UI Components: `src/components/`\\n- Tests: `src/__tests__/` and inline `__tests__/` directories\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 Next Steps\\n\\n1. Configure your Firebase project\\n2. Explore the flow builder at `/builder`\\n3. Check out the demo at `/demo`\\n4. Read the documentation in `/docs`\\n5. Start building your own flows!\\n\"}", "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_0176iCsbyLwMeNopDWaXg8W4", "id": null, "provider_details": null, "part_kind": "tool-call"}
