ents**:\\n- Overview and architecture\\n- Library selection rationale\\n- Installation instructions\\n- Usage examples (3 different scenarios)\\n- Processing pipeline visualization\\n- Feature matrix (supported markdown & DOCX features)\\n- Configuration guide\\n- Error handling patterns\\n- Comparison with original implementation\\n- Migration guide\\n- Performance considerations\\n- Testing guidelines\\n- Troubleshooting guide\\n- Future enhancement ideas\\n- Version history\\n\\n## \ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f Architecture\\n\\n### Processing Pipeline\\n```\\nUser Input (Markdown or Project)\\n    \u2193\\nProcess PlantUML Diagrams (optional)\\n    \u2193\\nGenerate Markdown (if Project object)\\n    \u2193\\nParse with remark + GFM\\n    \u2193\\nConvert to DOCX via remark-docx plugin\\n    \u2193\\nGenerate ArrayBuffer\\n    \u2193\\nConvert to Buffer (server) or Blob (client)\\n```\\n\\n### File Structure\\n```\\nsrc/lib/\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 markdown-to-docx-external.ts    \u2190 NEW (external library based)\\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 markdown-to-word-converter.ts   \u2190 EXISTING (custom implementation)\\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 ...\\ndocs/\\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 MARKDOWN_TO_DOCX_EXTERNAL_CONVERTER.md  \u2190 NEW (comprehensive docs)\\n```\\n\\n## \u2728 Key Advantages Over Custom Implementation\\n\\n| Aspect | Custom (Original) | External (New) |\\n|--------|-------------------|----------------|\\n| Code Lines | ~655 lines | ~370 lines |\\n| Complexity | High | Low |\\n| Maintenance | Manual | Community-maintained |\\n| Dependencies | docx library | remark-docx (includes docx) |\\n| Advanced Features | Limited | Built-in (Mermaid, Math, etc.) |\\n| Integration | Standalone | Unified ecosystem |\\n| Testing | Manual | Library-tested |\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd0c Integration Points\\n\\n### Direct Replacement Scenarios\\nThe new converter can replace the old one in:\\n- DOCX export API endpoints\\n- Project-to-document workflows\\n- Markdown-to-document conversions\\n- Dynamic document g